    "body": "My inclination is that this is just part of learning how to read specs. Sometimes, a single step is long, and takes more than a single paragraph to explain how it works. The additional paragraphs are not substeps, because they don't happen in sequence, and are not nested under a condition (e.g., \"if\") or loop (e.g., \"while\"). They are just expanding on the step that you're currently reading.\n\nArguably the final sentence, \"When no more bytes are available...\", could be made into a separate step, but I think it's still more accurate to describe it as just part of the whole byte-processing step.",
